WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:09.600
Begin with the brand board. This walkthrough presents design concepts for review.

2
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:19.600
The system board explores visual foundations. Treat its proposals as design direction.

3
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:29.600
The showcase board explores presentation. Its imagery is not benchmark evidence.

4
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:39.600
The hero board explores an introduction. Read product promises against their sources.

5
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:49.600
The lab board explores interactions. A demonstration does not qualify a deployment.

6
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:59.600
The marketing board explores a story. Customer outcomes require separate evidence.

7
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:09.600
The console board is a concept. Its displays do not establish live service operations.

8
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:19.600
The docs board explores navigation. Discuss a scoped project and review the evidence.

9
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.400
What kind of help fits?

10
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.800
Make the style explicit.

11
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.700
Three profiles in ABI.

12
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.600
ABI. Orchestration and routing.

13
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.600
Aviva. Direct, technical, candid.

14
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.600
Abbey. Conversational, empathetic, technical.

15
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:50.400
An explicit address can select a profile.

16
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.400
Bring your project’s scope.

17
00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.800
We’ll review its evidence.

18
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.400
I’m Abbey, the conversational profile.

19
00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.600
Quesar. Private AI operations. Evidence first.

20
00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.500
ABI has a local keyword routing path.

21
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.900
An explicit persona address can bypass scoring.

22
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.600
Three distinct profiles.

23
00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:24.300
WDBX: snapshots, recovery, vector search.

24
00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.900
Audit blocks hash predecessor links and metadata.

25
00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.600
Strict checks recompute hashes. Links alone do not.

26
00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.100
ABI’s scoped audit uses thirteen phrase patterns.

27
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.700
Six principles contribute to its audit score.

28
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.600
Pattern checks do not establish semantic truth.

29
00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.900
A distributed cognitive fabric remains our vision.

30
00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.600
Compatibility still needs qualification.

31
00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.400
Bring a defined problem and an evidence requirement.

32
00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.600
Discuss your project. Review the scope together.

33
00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.200
Answers are a starting point.

34
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.700
Ask what supports the claim.

35
00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.700
Follow the source.

36
00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.200
Keep component boundaries visible.

37
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:29.900
WDBX has CPU primitives: dot products, norms, cosine and top-k.

38
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:38.100
Accelerator capability states separate availability, initialization, execution and runtime verification.

39
00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:46.900
The durable store integrates snapshots, write-ahead recovery and HNSW search.

40
00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:54.100
WAL frames checksum JSON bytes. Bad checksums report corruption.

41
00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:03.400
Recovery treats an incomplete final frame differently from a bad checksum.

42
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:11.100
Store-facing completion persistence belongs to MCP, outside the pure AI core.

43
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.700
Three persona profiles.

44
00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.600
Abbey.

45
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.400
Aviva.

46
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.300
Abi.

47
00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:29.900
The local router adjusts weights using keyword prefixes, then selects a profile.

48
00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:37.700
An explicit leading persona address bypasses that scoring path.

49
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:49.400
Abbey combines conversation and technical care. Aviva leads directly. ABI handles orchestration.

50
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:58.700
The training path records metadata and profile vectors; model weights remain unchanged.

51
00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.300
Inspect the integrity boundary.

52
00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:10.900
A block hash includes its predecessor, timestamp, sequence, profile and metadata.

53
00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:18.700
That SHA-256 construction is a hash chain, not a digital signature.

54
00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:23.700
Strict checks recompute hashes; link-only checks do not.

55
00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:32.900
ABI’s audit matches thirteen case-insensitive patterns and scores six principles.

56
00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:39.700
Responses avoiding those phrases can escape its checks.

57
00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:49.000
Source inspection establishes what is implemented, with runtime qualification still separate.

58
00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:56.700
Ask for the test, the environment, and the precise scope behind a result.

59
00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:01.700
Broader reasoning is a research direction.

60
00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.300
Keep the roadmap visible.

61
00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:14.000
Our vision is a distributed cognitive fabric.

62
00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:23.700
That vision does not establish support across every device or hardware tier.

63
00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:29.700
Compatibility needs execution evidence on each intended path.

64
00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:40.400
A proposed direction becomes an engineering task when its acceptance evidence is defined.

65
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:52.700
For a project, define the workload, data boundary, failure behavior and review process before promising delivery.

66
00:06:54.000 --> 00:07:06.700
Start with a bounded question. Name the source, inspect the implementation, and agree how the result will be checked.

67
00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:21.400
These equations illustrate concepts. They do not establish a benchmark, semantic truth or a deployment guarantee.

68
00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:38.700
Use the illustration to frame questions: which inputs matter, which assumptions hold, and what evidence would change the decision?

69
00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.700
Bring a scoped project.

70
00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:47.600
Let’s review the evidence together.

71
00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.300
Quesar. Private AI operations.

72
00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:57.600
Follow the boundaries, one idea at a time.

73
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:04.100
ABI separates its pure AI core from storage I/O.

74
00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:10.300
MCP owns the store-facing completion persistence tail.

75
00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:15.600
Vector primitives and accelerator contracts.

76
00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:23.300
The durable store integrates snapshots, WAL recovery and HNSW search.

77
00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:30.600
Recovery can report corruption or I/O failure. Durability has limits.

78
00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:35.500
Audit blocks carry predecessor hashes.

79
00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:41.300
The block hash covers time, sequence, profile and metadata.

80
00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:47.600
Strict verification recomputes content hashes. Link-only verification does not.

81
00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:55.300
Abbey, Aviva and ABI are persona profiles with identity contracts.

82
00:08:55.600 --> 00:09:03.600
Keyword routing is a local path. Explicit leading names can select a profile.

83
00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.700
Abbey: conversational.

84
00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.700
Aviva: direct, technical.

85
00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.700
Abi: routing.

86
00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:19.700
The scoped audit matches thirteen case-insensitive phrase patterns.

87
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:24.700
Six principles contribute, including safety and privacy.

88
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:28.600
Harm outside those phrases can escape detection.

89
00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:36.300
A distributed cognitive fabric is a longer-term vision.

90
00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:41.900
Compatibility and delivery require separate qualification.

91
00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:47.600
Treat the roadmap as a direction, with questions still open.

92
00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.300
Begin with a defined project.

93
00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:59.600
Discuss the scope, inspect the sources, and agree on the evidence needed.
